{id:'CTRL-1259',name:'Operations — Review and sign-off',text:'The Operational Controls and Governance Assurance team performs segregation of duties reviews across all critical processes, confirming that no individual holds conflicting responsibilities and that approval levels are appropriately separated (on a monthly basis for standing governance oversight reviews and quarterly for comprehensive policy and segregation of duties assessments across all in-scope business areas, within the firm\'s governance framework, covering all board and management committee processes, approval chains, policy oversight mechanisms and regulatory compliance controls), to provide independent assurance to the board that governance policies, approval mechanisms and oversight arrangements are operating effectively and in compliance with regulatory requirements, by applying structured governance review checklists, sampling key approval decisions and control outputs, and issuing governance audit reports with rated findings to the Audit and Risk Committee for review and sign-off.',area:'Operations',type:'Automated',owner:'I. Ferreira',lastAssessed:'2021-05-25',who:1,what:1,where:0,how:1,when:1,why:0,score:4}
